{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a delivery sends events: a plain sink that records the batches it receives."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Destination"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives each destination its batches in the order the events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"were tracked, one at a time: the next batch comes once ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns. Batches that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arrive meanwhile wait in a buffer of the destination’s own, which drops its oldest batch when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full, so a destination that falls behind loses batches rather than holding up the others.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)"},{"text":" should return promptly and honour cancellation: a delivery waits for it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before it completes, and cancels it when the delivery is cancelled. A destination handles its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own errors (a failed upload, say); the delivery has none to receive.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a tracker keeps its records i